IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sa-part3-general`

-- Part 10 and Schedule 1 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia).
-- Section 60 is a power of the Governor to make regulations and has no entry here.
-- Clauses 24 and 25 of Schedule 1 are transitional.
-- The day section 19 commenced and the day the Act commenced are each an input.

§ `Part 10 and Schedule 1 -- Miscellaneous and transitional provisions`

§§ `Schedule 1, clause 24 -- Bills introduced before commencement of section 19`

-- src:635 | (2) In this clause—
-- src:636 | amending provision of an Act means a provision of an Act that amends another Act.
@ref cl 24(2) (src:635-636)
GIVEN `the provision amends another Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision of an Act is an amending provision` MEANS
    `the provision amends another Act`

-- Section 28 makes a provision operate from the beginning of its commencement day.
-- A Bill introduced on that day is therefore introduced after section 19 commenced, so only an earlier day is "before".
-- src:634 | (1) Despite section 19, section headings to amending provisions do not form part of an Act if the Bill for that Act was introduced in either House of Parliament before the commencement of section 19 (regardless of whether the Bill passes the Parliament, or comes into operation, after the commencement of section 19).
@ref cl 24(1) (src:634)
GIVEN `the heading is a section heading to an amending provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Bill for the Act was introduced in either House of Parliament` IS A DATE
      `the day section 19 commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a section heading to an amending provision forms part of the Act` MEANS
    IF `the heading is a section heading to an amending provision`
       AND (Day `the day the Bill for the Act was introduced in either House of Parliament`) LESS THAN (Day `the day section 19 commenced`)
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `a thing appearing in an Act or legislative instrument is part of it` `anything else appearing in it`

§§ `Schedule 1, clause 25 -- References to time`

-- The input below is the period's own commencement day, whatever kind of instrument it arises under.
-- src:638 | Section 44 does not operate to alter the period of time provided or allowed for the doing of anything under an Act or a statutory instrument if the period commenced before the commencement of this Act.
@ref cl 25 (src:638)
GIVEN `the day the period of time commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the Act commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 44 operates to alter the period of time provided or allowed for the doing of the thing` MEANS
    IF (Day `the day the period of time commenced`) LESS THAN (Day `the day the Act commenced`) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Tests`

#ASSERT `a provision of an Act is an amending provision` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision of an Act is an amending provision` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Bill introduced the day before section 19 commenced: the heading is not part of the Act.
#ASSERT `a section heading to an amending provision forms part of the Act` TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS FALSE
-- Bill introduced on the day section 19 commenced: introduced after commencement, so section 19 decides.
#ASSERT `a section heading to an amending provision forms part of the Act` TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a section heading to an amending provision forms part of the Act` TRUE (Date 2 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS TRUE
-- Not a heading to an amending provision: clause 24 does not touch it.
#ASSERT `a section heading to an amending provision forms part of the Act` FALSE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 44 operates to alter the period of time provided or allowed for the doing of the thing` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 44 operates to alter the period of time provided or allowed for the doing of the thing` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 44 operates to alter the period of time provided or allowed for the doing of the thing` (Date 2 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
